{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1540117-tc-aeon-large-scale-combat-for-vtts","id":1540117,"title":"[TC Aeon] Large Scale Combat for VTTs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-09T19:27:21-07:00","id":1540117,"title":"[TC Aeon] Large Scale Combat for VTTs","content":"I <i>very</i> like <b>Large Scale Combat</b> rules from Taste Bit. Ideas for running mass combat scenes in space is very like my jam I'm here for <b>Aeon</b>. But I have a one big problem with rules as written - I'm proponent on running combat scenes on Virtual TableTops. I think that <b>LSC</b> not work for them as written. Here is quick patch to make it possible.<br /> <br /> For any one not sure - we talk about<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/pl/product/472323/trinity-continuum-large-scale-comba\" target=\"_blank\"><b> rules addition for this mini-supplement</b></a><br /> <br /> <img width=\"224\" height=\"320\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/4261/472323.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/4261/472323.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/4261/472323.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Large Scale Combat for VTTs </b><br /> <br /> <i><b>Assuming that each Fleet LSU </b>is reflecting moderate to small invading in world Fleet ( up to circa 20 ships ) we made <b>approximation of each Health level to number of ships on each side</b>. ( Rounded down ) Assuming that normal Chromatic Fleet have around 20 ships - and having in mind that Chromatics like to work in 3s - we decide numer of ships by Health levels LSU have, to have 'ships-to-Health levels' numbers. We get about '3 ships per Health' so we deploy those on battle map accordingly. Each lose Health level for the Chromatics Fleet is 3 ships that we take out of battle map.</i>\ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> And that's all. How do you feel on this patch? What should be 'ships-to-Health' ration for Earth's Defense Forces? Orgotek ships armada? Waiting for you comments. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-09-2024, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T19:51:36-07:00","id":1542602,"title":"","content":"<b>Speed and Maneuverability</b> - Each element of particular LSU Fleet can move up to Speed in Squares or Hexes per combat turn. Massive or defensive parts of Fleet - like Mother Ship or Cruiser - can move up to 2/3 of Fleets Speed per turn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}